      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّ اَلْمُؤْمِنَ يَخْشَعُ لَهُ كُلُّ شَيْ‌ءٍ ثُمَّ قَالَ ع إِذَا كَانَ مُخْلِصاً قَلْبَهُ لِلَّهِ أَخَافَ اَللَّهُ مِنْهُ كُلَّ شَيْ‌ءٍ حَتَّى هَوَامَّ اَلْأَرْضِ وَ سِبَاعَهَا وَ طَيْرَ اَلسَّمَاءِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.badr-shahin": [
          "(The same previous series of relaters)… from Mohammed bin Ahmed from … Safwan al-Jammal that he heard Abu Abdullah (a) saying: Everything is submissive to the believer. He (a) then added: Allah will cause everything, including vermin, beasts, and birds, to fear the believer if he is sincere to Allah."
        ]
      }
